{"id":"mahabharata-8-061","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · Bhima kills Duhshasana","summary":{"en":"Duhshasana performs a hard feat in the battle and cuts Bhima's arrows, but Bhima throws his mace and fells him. Bhima drinks his blood as he vowed, and roars that he has fulfilled his oath for the insult to Draupadi.","kn":"ದುಃಶಾಸನ ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಠಿಣ ಸಾಹಸ ತೋರಿ ಭೀಮನ ಬಾಣ ಕತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಗದೆ ಎಸೆದು ಅವನನ್ನು ಬೀಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆಯಂತೆ ಅವನ ರಕ್ತ ಕುಡಿದು ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ಅವಮಾನದ ಶಪಥ ಪೂರೈಸಿದೆನೆಂದು ಗರ್ಜಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुःशासन युद्ध में कठिन पराक्रम दिखाकर भीम के बाण काटता है, पर भीम गदा फेंककर उसे गिरा देते हैं। वे प्रतिज्ञा के अनुसार उसका रक्त पीते हैं और गरजते हैं कि द्रौपदी के अपमान की शपथ पूरी हुई।","te":"దుశ్శాసనుడు యుద్ధంలో కఠిన సాహసం చూపి భీముని బాణాలు ఛేదిస్తాడు; భీముడు గద విసిరి అతన్ని కూల్చుతాడు. ప్రతిజ్ఞ ప్రకారం అతని రక్తం తాగి ద్రౌపది అవమానానికి చేసిన ప్రతిజ్ఞ నెరవేరిందని గర్జిస్తాడు.","ta":"துச்சாசனன் போரில் கடினமாகப் போரிட்டு பீமனின் அம்புகளை வெட்ட, பீமன் கதை எறிந்து அவனை வீழ்த்துகிறான். சபதப்படி அவன் இரத்தத்தைக் குடித்துத் திரௌபதியின் அவமானத்துக்கான சபதம் நிறைவேறியது என்று முழங்குகிறான்.","ml":"ദുശ്ശാസനൻ യുദ്ധത്തിൽ കടുത്ത വിരുതു കാണിക്കുകയും ഭീമന്റെ അമ്പുകൾ മുറിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു; എന്നാൽ ഭീമൻ ഗദയെറിഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വീഴ്ത്തുന്നു. താൻ പ്രതിജ്ഞ ചെയ്തതുപോലെ ഭീമൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ രക്തം കുടിക്കുന്നു; ദ്രൗപദിയെ അപമാനിച്ചതിന് പ്രതിജ്ഞ നിറവേറ്റിയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ഗർജ്ജിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तत्राकरोद्दुष्करं राजपुत्रो\nदुःशासनस्तुमुले युध्यमानः ।\nचिच्छेद भीमस्य धनुः क्षुरेण\nषड्भिः शरैः सारथिमप्यविध्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There prince Duhshasana, fighting in the melee, did a hard deed: he cut Bhima's bow with a razor-headed arrow and pierced his charioteer with six arrows."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततोऽभिनद्बहुभिः क्षिप्रमेव\nवरेषुभिर्भीमसेनं महात्मा ।\nस विक्षरन्नाग इव प्रभिन्नो\nगदामस्मै तुमुले प्राहिणोद्वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled Duhshasana quickly pierced Bhimasena with many excellent arrows; Bhima, like an elephant streaming rut-fluid, hurled a mace at him in the fray."}},{"n":3,"text":"तयाहरद्दश धन्वन्तराणि\nदुःशासनं भीमसेनः प्रसह्य ।\nतया हतः पतितो वेपमानो\nदुःशासनो गदया वेगवत्या ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that mace Bhimasena forcibly flung Duhshasana a distance of ten bow-lengths; struck down by the swift mace, Duhshasana fell, trembling."}},{"n":4,"text":"हयाः ससूताश्च हता नरेन्द्र\nचूर्णीकृतश्चास्य रथः पतन्त्या ।\nविध्वस्तवर्माभरणाम्बरस्र-\nग्विचेष्टमानो भृशवेदनार्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, his horses and charioteer were slain and his chariot was ground to pieces by the falling mace; with his armor, ornaments, garments and garland torn apart, he writhed, racked with pain."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः स्मृत्वा भीमसेनस्तरस्वी\nसापत्नकं यत्प्रयुक्तं सुतैस्ते ।\nरथादवप्लुत्य गतः स भूमौ\nयत्नेन तस्मिन्प्रणिधाय चक्षुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Bhimasena, remembering the hostile deeds done to him by your sons, leapt down from his chariot to the ground, fixing his gaze on Duhshasana with intent."}},{"n":6,"text":"असिं समुद्धृत्य शितं सुधारं\nकण्ठे समाक्रम्य च वेपमानम् ।\nउत्कृत्य वक्षः पतितस्य भूमा-\nवथापिबच्छोणितमस्य कोष्णम् ।\nआस्वाद्य चास्वाद्य च वीक्षमाणः\nक्रुद्धोऽतिवेलं प्रजगाद वाक्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drawing a sharp, keen-edged sword and pressing on the trembling man's throat as he lay fallen on the ground, he tore open his chest and drank his warm blood; tasting it again and again and looking on, he spoke in great anger."}},{"n":7,"text":"स्तन्यस्य मातुर्मधुसर्पिषो वा\nमाध्वीकपानस्य च सत्कृतस्य ।\nदिव्यस्य वा तोयरसस्य पाना-\nत्पयोदधिभ्यां मथिताच्च मुख्यात् ।\nसर्वेभ्य एवाभ्यधिको रसोऽयं\nमतो ममाद्याहितलोहितस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Mother's milk, honey and ghee, well-prepared honey wine, divine waters, milk, curds and the finest churned butter: this taste, as I judge it today from my enemy's blood, is better than all of them.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एवं ब्रुवाणं पुनराद्रवन्त-\nमास्वाद्य वल्गन्तमतिप्रहृष्टम् ।\nये भीमसेनं ददृशुस्तदानीं\nभयेन तेऽपि व्यथिता निपेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even those who saw Bhimasena then, as he said this, tasted the blood, ran again at the fallen man and leapt about in great delight, fell down shaking in fear."}},{"n":9,"text":"ये चापि तत्रापतिता मनुष्या-\nस्तेषां करेभ्यः पतितं च शस्त्रम् ।\nभयाच्च संचुक्रुशुरुच्चकैस्ते\nनिमीलिताक्षा ददृशुश्च तन्न ॥","meaning":{"en":"The men who were there let their weapons fall from their hands; in terror they cried out loudly, shut their eyes, and could not look at it."}},{"n":10,"text":"ये तत्र भीमं ददृशुः समन्ता-\nद्दौःशासनं तद्रुधिरं पिबन्तम् ।\nसर्वे पलायन्त भयाभिपन्ना\nनायं मनुष्य इति भाषमाणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All who saw Bhima on every side drinking Duhshasana's blood fled in terror, saying, \"This is not a man.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"शृण्वतां लोकवीराणामिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nएष ते रुधिरं कण्ठात्पिबामि पुरुषाधम ।\nब्रूहीदानीं सुसंरब्धः पुनर्गौरिति गौरिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the hearing of the world's heroes he said this: \"I am drinking your blood from your throat, lowest of men. Now, in your fury, say again, 'Cow! Cow!'\""}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रमाणकोट्यां शयनं कालकूटस्य भोजनम् ।\nदशनं चाहिभिः कष्टं दाहं च जतुवेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sleeping at Pramanakoti, the poison Kalakuta as food, bites by snakes, the burning in the house of lac,"}},{"n":13,"text":"द्यूतेन राज्यहरणमरण्ये वसतिश्च या ।\nइष्वस्त्राणि च संग्रामेष्वसुखानि च वेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"the taking of our kingdom by dice, living in the forest, the painful arrows and weapons in battles, and the unhappiness in the king's palace:"}},{"n":14,"text":"दुःखान्येतानि जानीमो न सुखानि कदाचन ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य दौरात्म्यात्सपुत्रस्य सदा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"these we know as sorrows, never as joys; we have always had them because of the wickedness of Dhritarashtra and his sons.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा वचनं राजञ्जयं प्राप्य वृकोदरः ।\nपुनराह महाराज स्मयंस्तौ केशवार्जुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, having spoken these words and gained his victory, Vrikodara, smiling, spoke again, great king, to those two, Keshava and Arjuna."}},{"n":16,"text":"दुःशासने यद्रणे संश्रुतं मे\nतद्वै सर्वं कृतमद्येह वीरौ ।\nअद्यैव दास्याम्यपरं द्वितीयं\nदुर्योधनं यज्ञपशुं विशस्य ।\nशिरो मृदित्वा च पदा दुरात्मनः\nशान्तिं लप्स्ये कौरवाणां समक्षम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Heroes, everything I swore in the battle about Duhshasana has been accomplished here today. Today I will give the second as well, cutting down Duryodhana like a sacrificial animal; and trampling the head of that wicked man with my foot, I will find peace in front of the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा वचनं प्रहृष्टो\nननाद चोच्चै रुधिरार्द्रगात्रः ।\nननर्त चैवातिबलो महात्मा\nवृत्रं निहत्येव सहस्रनेत्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this much, filled with joy, his body wet with blood, he roared loudly; the mighty, great-souled Bhima danced, as thousand-eyed Indra did on slaying Vritra."}}]}]}